"Probably the Chinese"?

239
00:10:58,991 --> 00:11:00,451
Were you really thinking that?

240
00:11:00,534 --> 00:11:01,410
I... I...

241
00:11:01,494 --> 00:11:03,120
-When we...
-I did... I did think it.

242
00:11:03,204 --> 00:11:06,707
I did think as a racist cliché, yes.

243
00:11:06,791 --> 00:11:10,961
As a culturally, uh, un-PC cliché...

244
00:11:11,045 --> 00:11:12,171
-Right.
-...yes.

245
00:11:12,713 --> 00:11:14,382
-[sighs]
-But I don't believe it.

246
00:11:14,465 --> 00:11:16,842
-No, I don't either.
-No. [chuckles]

247
00:11:16,926 --> 00:11:18,219
-It's...
-'Cause we're not racist.

248
00:11:18,302 --> 00:11:19,136
No.

249
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:21,847
-And certainly not against the Chinese.
-No.

250
00:11:21,931 --> 00:11:23,099
[Jerry laughs]

251
00:11:26,894 --> 00:11:27,812
No sunglasses.

252
00:11:27,895 --> 00:11:30,147
-Well...
-The eyes are your genius,

253
00:11:30,231 --> 00:11:31,315
that's your magic.

254
00:11:31,690 --> 00:11:34,860
You're the only person
in the history of the show

255
00:11:34,944 --> 00:11:37,905
that has given me a hard time
about the sunglasses. The only one.

256
00:11:39,740 --> 00:11:40,991
And I care why?

257
00:11:41,075 --> 00:11:42,284
[Jerry laughs]

258
00:11:52,044 --> 00:11:55,798
You take the fake documentary away
and The Office is quite a boring show.

259
00:11:56,090 --> 00:11:57,091
Uh-huh.

260
00:11:57,174 --> 00:11:59,760
'Cause it's just an idiot being stupid
and people not caring.

261
00:11:59,844 --> 00:12:01,345
-I see. So that--
-So, once you know

262
00:12:01,429 --> 00:12:04,557
he's trying to be discovered,
"Everyone will love me."

263
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:06,225
-"Everyone will love me."
-Right.

264
00:12:06,308 --> 00:12:08,728
You know, it suddenly...
it brings it to life.

265
00:12:09,061 --> 00:12:11,522
Comedy is a normal guy, or gal,

266
00:12:12,106 --> 00:12:16,235
a normal person trying to do something
they're not equipped to do.

267
00:12:16,318 --> 00:12:18,070
-Right. Right.
-That's what we're laughing at.

268
00:12:18,154 --> 00:12:21,657
And the bigger their blind spot,
the more exciting it is.

269
00:12:21,741 --> 00:12:24,368
And I just try to take it to nth degree
with David Brent.

270
00:12:24,452 --> 00:12:27,705
So the build was his blind spot.
And you do it with a fake documentary.

271
00:12:27,788 --> 00:12:30,249
So now, he can say something
to the camera,

272
00:12:30,332 --> 00:12:32,501
and then we can see that's not true.

273
00:12:32,585 --> 00:12:35,337
That's very, very, very brilliant.

274
00:12:39,425 --> 00:12:41,719
Why the V? Why do you like the V?

275
00:12:41,802 --> 00:12:43,679
-You always have a V.
-I don't know.

276
00:12:43,762 --> 00:12:45,097
You don't like a crew.

277
00:12:45,181 --> 00:12:46,682
-I always see you in a V.
-Yeah.

278
00:12:46,766 --> 00:12:48,601
-Why the V?
-I think it makes me

279
00:12:48,684 --> 00:12:50,144
look like I've got a neck.

280
00:12:50,352 --> 00:12:51,437
[laughs]

281
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:54,231
It's a little bits of vanity.

282
00:12:57,151 --> 00:12:59,570
Is there anything... 
Is there a comedic gift

283
00:12:59,653 --> 00:13:02,406
that you would love to have,

284
00:13:02,490 --> 00:13:04,825
but you don't quite possess?

285
00:13:04,909 --> 00:13:07,119
Well, I suppose it's the people
I've stolen from.

286
00:13:07,203 --> 00:13:08,829
-Right.
-Like, I tried to get 

287
00:13:08,913 --> 00:13:11,582
a bit of the humanity
from Laurel and Hardy.

288
00:13:11,665 --> 00:13:14,752
These two idiots, they both thought
the other one was a bigger idiot.

289
00:13:18,047 --> 00:13:18,964
Look at that.

290
00:13:22,259 --> 00:13:23,552
How do you like that?

291
00:13:24,595 --> 00:13:25,888
Is that what you wanted?

292
00:13:28,015 --> 00:13:29,767
-[Jerry laughs]
-It's what I've got.

293
00:13:29,892 --> 00:13:31,519
[both laugh]

294
00:13:36,106 --> 00:13:38,484
The nearer to the punchline
you have to think about something,

295
00:13:38,567 --> 00:13:39,902
-the worse it is.
-Right.

296
00:13:39,985 --> 00:13:41,612
Just if someone shouts something out,

297
00:13:41,695 --> 00:13:44,114
the closer you are to the punchline,
you got to start again.

298
00:13:44,198 --> 00:13:45,574
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

299
00:13:45,658 --> 00:13:48,035
Sometimes you get interrupted
in the middle of something.

300
00:13:48,118 --> 00:13:51,080
I say, "Did you ever see that thing
where there's, like, a train going by

301
00:13:51,163 --> 00:13:53,707
and there's one empty car,
and there's a guy with a motorcycle

302
00:13:53,791 --> 00:13:56,710
and he goes through 
when he jumps through that space?"

303
00:13:56,794 --> 00:13:59,463
-I go, "That's what a joke is."
-That's exactly it.

304
00:13:59,547 --> 00:14:02,383
Once that train goes by,
I can't jump my motorcycle anymore.

305
00:14:02,466 --> 00:14:04,677
Yeah. I think I said, it was like, um...

306
00:14:05,219 --> 00:14:06,971
-hitting the golf ball.
-Uh-huh.

307
00:14:07,054 --> 00:14:09,473
That you're okay... 
You can be interrupted there...

308
00:14:10,724 --> 00:14:12,142
[both laughing]

309
00:14:13,102 --> 00:14:16,522
-That's great.
-...but not there. You go...

310
00:14:20,693 --> 00:14:23,070
I did this joke,  I came out to the crowd,

311
00:14:23,654 --> 00:14:24,822
and I said, uh,

312
00:14:25,364 --> 00:14:26,740
"Eighteen years sober."

313
00:14:27,199 --> 00:14:30,828
And they gave me a round of applause.
And I went, "The first 18 years."

314
00:14:31,829 --> 00:14:34,456
Since then, I've been drunk 
every night of my life.

315
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:35,499
-Right?
-That's funny.

316
00:14:35,583 --> 00:14:36,834
The paper picked it up...

317
00:14:37,376 --> 00:14:39,628
and put, "Ricky Gervais admits
to being drunk

318
00:14:39,878 --> 00:14:41,630
every night of his life, from 18."

319
00:14:41,714 --> 00:14:44,049
And now the big question,
I think, the last couple years...

320
00:14:44,133 --> 00:14:46,302
It's always been around,
but the last couple of years is,

321
00:14:46,385 --> 00:14:48,012
you know, the fight for freedom of speech.

322
00:14:48,095 --> 00:14:50,264
-I joke about really terrible things.
-Yeah.

323
00:14:50,848 --> 00:14:53,100
-And I know they're terrible, of course.
-Of course.

324
00:14:53,183 --> 00:14:57,313
And whenever a new thing comes out
that's raw and sensitive,

325
00:14:57,396 --> 00:14:59,023
people say, "You don't understand."

326
00:14:59,106 --> 00:15:00,649
-I go, "No, I do understand."
-Of course.

327
00:15:00,733 --> 00:15:03,402
"I know this is bad.
I know the Holocaust was bad.

328
00:15:03,485 --> 00:15:04,612
I know AIDS is bad.

329
00:15:04,987 --> 00:15:07,948
It's the joking about it that
you don't like, 'cause it's your thing."

330
00:15:08,032 --> 00:15:11,118
I was saying about freedom of speech,
you should be able to joke about anything.

331
00:15:11,201 --> 00:15:13,787
And they say things like, um,
"Oh, you agree with Hitler, then."

332
00:15:13,871 --> 00:15:16,040
I go, "Well, no, it wasn't so much
what he said."

333
00:15:16,123 --> 00:15:17,291
-Right.
-"It's what he did."

334
00:15:17,374 --> 00:15:19,251
If he had just said [bleep] things...

335
00:15:20,961 --> 00:15:22,630
It would've been a lot better
for all of us.

336
00:15:22,713 --> 00:15:25,633
Our fight for the right
to joke about anything--

337
00:15:25,716 --> 00:15:27,801
Do you think it's ebbing away 
in this culture?

338
00:15:27,885 --> 00:15:30,012
This is the thing about freedom of speech.

339
00:15:30,095 --> 00:15:32,890
Um, everyone agrees with it
until they hear something they don't like.

340
00:15:34,350 --> 00:15:38,228
So, do we leave that China joke in or not?

341
00:15:39,396 --> 00:15:40,564
[Jerry] What will they do?

342
00:15:40,648 --> 00:15:42,316
-If you were quoted out of context...
-Yeah.

343
00:15:42,399 --> 00:15:44,401
[Jerry] Do they risk
offending the Chinese?

344
00:15:44,485 --> 00:15:45,944
...it would be very, very unfair.

345
00:15:46,028 --> 00:15:48,739
How could you possibly win
against the massive population...

346
00:15:48,822 --> 00:15:49,657
[Jerry] It's tricky!

347
00:15:49,740 --> 00:15:50,783
It's so subjective.

348
00:15:50,866 --> 00:15:51,825
[Jerry] It's sticky.

349
00:15:51,909 --> 00:15:53,202
I could never hurt the Chinese.

350
00:15:53,285 --> 00:15:54,411
[Jerry] It's Ricky.

351
00:15:54,495 --> 00:15:56,914
You don't really think all Chinese people
are the same?

352
00:15:56,997 --> 00:15:58,916
-No. 
-What if people make comments

353
00:15:58,999 --> 00:15:59,833
on the Internet?

354
00:15:59,917 --> 00:16:01,794
'Cause you're offended
doesn't mean you're right.

355
00:16:01,877 --> 00:16:03,212
[Jerry] Is there any way out?

356
00:16:03,295 --> 00:16:05,005
-You can go to jail.
-Hate crime?

357
00:16:05,089 --> 00:16:06,840
[Jerry] Stay tuned
for the exciting conclusion

358
00:16:06,924 --> 00:16:09,593
of Ricky Gervais, "China, maybe?"

359
00:16:09,843 --> 00:16:13,138
-Same Comedians in Cars time.
-You're the one that looks the idiot.

360
00:16:13,222 --> 00:16:15,891
Same Comedians in Cars channel.

